// REJECTS: Field 'region' is required
//
// An Athena specification with database, workGroup and outputLocation but no `region`.
// athenaDatasourceSpecification is a `( ... )*` alternation over six optional elements, so
// this parses cleanly and the requirement is applied by the walker afterwards.
//
// Athena is the one vendor in this batch with no host and no port -- it is addressed by
// `region` plus an S3 `outputLocation` -- so `region` here is not a convenience label but the
// endpoint itself, and its being required is the analogue of `host` being required elsewhere.
// A rewrite reading the .g4 alone finds every field optional and accepts an unaddressable
// connection.
//
// `athenaEndpoint` is the optional override and is deliberately absent below: supplying it
// does not satisfy the requirement, which is what makes the check a fixed one rather than a
// one-of-these-two.
###Connection
RelationalDatabaseConnection fixture::neg::AthenaMissingRegion
{
  store: fixture::neg::Db;
  type: Athena;
  specification: Athena
  {
    database: 'dbname';
    workGroup: 'workGroupX';
    outputLocation: 's3://bucket/prefix';
  };
  auth: Test;
}
